<Page title="About VolleyballTech" description="Who is behind VolleyballTech, how we research gear and what you can expect from us.">
  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Buying volleyball gear is confusing. Product pages are full of marketing terms, and most advice is written
    for elite players. VolleyballTech is for everyone else: recreational players, club and school athletes,
    parents and volunteer coaches who just want to know what is worth the money.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
  <p>
    VolleyballTech is an independent project run by a recreational player – not a former pro and not a brand.
    We think that is a useful point of view: we ask the same questions you do, and we do not pretend to know
    more than we do.
  </p>

  <h2>How we research</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Specs first.</strong> We collect checkable specs and compare products side by side.</li>
    <li><strong>Clear labels.</strong> Every product page says whether we used the product ourselves or relied on research.</li>
    <li><strong>Both sides.</strong> Every recommendation includes who should skip it.</li>
    <li><strong>Corrections welcome.</strong> If you spot a mistake, tell us and we will fix it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The full method is on our <a href="/how-we-research/">how we research gear</a> page.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>
    Some links are affiliate links. Read the details in our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
